## TRI7 ecosystem packaging (all repos migrated + graded B)
- tridock: tri7.Dockerfile (multi-stage rust build of tri7d, non-root, tor bundled, full/seed/staking modes, staking mode refuses without mounted wallet) → image samiahmed7777/tridock:tri7 on Docker Hub; legacy preserved as :legacy. build-and-publish.yml builds tri7.Dockerfile with `build-contexts: tri7=<checkout path>` (the Dockerfile consumes a tri7 build context — Actions needs a checkout step + build-contexts, or buildx pulls 'tri7' as a nonexistent image).
- tri-pi: real aarch64 tri7d binaries + native ubuntu-24.04-arm CI builder; VERSION v7.0.0-tri7.1.
- tri7 repo: trigger-tridock.yml workflow_dispatch → repository_dispatch tri-release-published → tridock (set TRIDOCK_DISPATCH_TOKEN on BOTH repos).
- Package managers: WinGet/Chocolatey/Homebrew/AUR shipped by distribute.yml on tag pushes (grade B urn:ump:cajdx3ohvsdnlxj3apyjmlyizarmlmvdal7wvsryyxdvok7l2pla) — full details in the "Distribution pipeline DONE" bullet above; judge round-1 C blockers worth remembering: a pinned-version install script (chocolateyInstall.ps1) must have its URL AND checksum rewritten by CI, and an AUR job MUST rewrite pkgver/sha256sums + regenerate .SRCINFO per release or the package silently goes stale.
- EXPLORER-VERB (2026-11-07, commit b0e9684, GLM B): native `richlist` verb + explicit `--balances` snapshot builder + GUI live-verb preference — see references/explorer-verb.md for the full rule set (atomic writes, snapshot-pair rebuild, archive-seam depth, aarch64 linker env var).
- KEYPOOLREFILL (2026-11-07, commits 35038b1+1ab867b, GLM A): native `keypoolrefill` + pool-backed getnewaddress + top-up maintainer + real getwalletinfo census — see references/keypool-and-refill.md for the pool-row byte spec, the replace-vs-add recount rule (imported pool indices can reach the HD counter), the pop key-row check, and the wallet-class map (DNS3/Pi imported, DNS2/PC HD).
- SWEEP-RESIDUE (2026-11-07, commit 871dbf3, GLM A): CLI sweep `--min-sats` residue floor (default 5000 sats = 0.005 TRI) — see references/tri7-cli-and-seed-tools.md for the floor rule, the CLI-only scope (GUI sweep_flow keeps move-everything), and the live two-pass completion proof (non-seed 582.25 → 0 TRI, staking never paused).

## Fleet / tooling
- Codex as UI-redesign SPEC WRITER (worked end-to-end): `cd <repo> && IS_SANDBOX=1 codex exec --sandbox workspace-write --skip-git-repo-check -i <brand-image-1> -i <brand-image-2> < /tmp/prompt.txt` — images attach via repeated `-i` flags (codex SEEES them), and the prompt MUST come from a FILE via stdin: a multi-line quoted prompt through the Hermes background wrapper gets mangled ('Reading prompt from stdin... No prompt provided'). Prompt shape that worked: sources-to-read first (brand images + legacy UI definitions + current implementation), spec sections enumerated, 'be decisive - the parent agent executes verbatim', and 'DO NOT modify source files; ONLY write <SPEC>.md'. Spec must include exact hex tables, current-vs-new comparisons, concrete egui/Visuals values, and asset regeneration steps — vague vibes specs are not executable. VALIDATED END-TO-END: the 502-line spec it produced was executed by a separate verbatim-execution agent (grade B, 9ecc283) under two constraints that made it work: (1) Codex writes ONLY the spec — asset generation delegated to the executor used ImageMagick, which produced mushy results for wordmark letterforms; Codex generating vector SVGs itself (paths/gradients, iterated with test rasterizations) is the better route for logo-grade art, and (2) the executor's hard rule 'ZERO logic changes — view layer + assets only' kept sends/staking/messaging byte-identical through a 4300-line view rewrite. Brand assets: Sami supplied the canonical banner image directly — the authentic supplied artwork beats any recreation for wordmark letterforms; recreation only won for the triangle mark.
